  "id": "grothendieck-infinity-groupoids-and-the-homotopy-hypothesis",
  "title": "Grothendieck infinity-groupoids and the homotopy hypothesis",
  "description": "Henry's pushout conjecture for every Grothendieck coherator, after OpenAI's 2026 proof: freely adjoining to a cellular infinity-groupoid a cell parallel to a given one, and a cell joining the two, is a weak equivalence. Globular theories and their models; the homotopy calculus; coskeletal cutoffs, spines and free shapes; trees and whiskers; partial cylinders and the main theorem; the canonical semi-model structure and the Quillen equivalence with spaces.",
